===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{context|computing|lang=en}} Playful solving of technical work that requires deep understanding, especially of a computer system.
#: From ''hacker'': ''"A person who delights in having an intimate understanding of the internal workings of a system, computers and computer networks in particular." &mdash; [http://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1392 RFC 1392]''
# {{context|computing|lang=en}} Unauthorized attempts to bypass the security mechanisms of an information system or network. See also [[cracker]].
# {{context|pathology|lang=en}} A dry [[coughing]]; the emission of a succession of short coughs.
# {{context|sports|chiefly|American football|soccer|rugby|lang=en}} A kick in the [[shin]]s.
# {{context|massage|lang=en}} The act of striking the muscles with the side of the hand.
# {{context|UK|countable|lang=en}} A riding or journey on [[horseback]]. (Plural [[hackings]].)
# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} The operation of working over the faces of rough or worn [[grindstone]]s with a hack-hammer.
# {{context|obsolete|masonry|lang=en}} The separation of a course of stones into two smaller courses, when there are not enough large stones to form a single course.
# {{context|obsolete|gem-cutting|lang=en}} The cuts and grooves made in the metal laps by holding the cutting edge of a steel blade against them while in motion, for the purpose of providing receptacles or pockets for the powders using in cutting  and polishing gems.
# {{context|obsolete|brick-making|lang=en}} The piling of bricks for drying.

